    "created_at": "2026-03-17T19:15:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-17T19:16:26Z",
    "body": "Also in general the behavior of an element's scoped registry (without shadow) is really strange IMO...\n\ne.g., the following wouldn't upgrade the element:\n```js\nconst customElementRegistry = new CustomElementRegistry()\ncustomElementRegistry.define(\"x-element\", \n  class MyElement extends HTMLElement { \n    constructor() { super(); console.log(\"ctor\"); }  \n  }\n);\n\nconst doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(\"<x-element></x-element>\", \"text/html\")\n\nconst container = document.createElement(\"div\", {customElementRegistry});\ndocument.body.append(container);\n\n// The element is adopted and connected, but wouldn't upgrade to anything.\ncontainer.append(doc.querySelector(\"x-element\"))\n```\n\nBut if you add `container.innerHTML = container.innerHTML` at the end, it would, because then the \"fragment parser takes custom element registry into account\" kicks in.\n\nThis feels non-obvious and unintuitive to me.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
